# Modules as directories (docs/modules-style-pass.md): top-level items that exist only for
# the tests live in a declared test module. `tests.prism` declares a helper type with its
# `derive` and a function over it; `more.prism`, a second test module, names them, as a
# test module may name another's helpers. Neither is read by `prism run`.
# Written by Claude on the claude-self-hosting branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod tests
test mod more
use Ui

Add: fn Nat, Nat -> Nat
fn Add a, b = a + b

@main: @unit
@main:
    Ui.Label(text=$"{Add 1, 2}")
